> The sample contains 55,190 country-resolution observations across 95 countries and 612 roll calls. Votes are scored -1 for no, 0 for abstain, and 1 for yes. The outcome is \(Y_{ir}=|s_{ir}-s_{Cr}|-|s_{ir}-s_{Ur}|\), where \(s_{Cr}\) and \(s_{Ur}\) are China's and the United States' scores; negative values indicate a vote closer to China. Country-resolution pairs without a recorded yes, no, or abstain vote -- whether because of absence, nonparticipation, or another reason -- do not enter the observed-vote sample. A resolution enters the China-U.S. divergent sample only when both China and the United States have recorded votes and their scores differ. Each observed vote is weighted equally, and the models include year fixed effects, country fixed effects, and issue-area fixed effects.
